    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d429">

                <pb facs="0545" n="477" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg477"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72/2140½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-09-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">10 September, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I do not think any
                    answer to this despatch is necessary.<anchor n="54" xml:id="d429-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>It is no doubt useful to know what opinion is on the other side of the water.
                    After while even Englishmen will begin to understand (I wonder if they really
                    ever will?) that what we are guided by is our sense of what is just and right
                    and not our sensibility as regards what other nations think about us.</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
